<title>USA: Amtran unit gets aircraft financing.</title>
<headline>Amtran unit gets aircraft financing.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amtran Inc said Thursday that its American Trans Air Inc unit secured $119.7 million in financing for aircraft and jet engines, with terms ranging from nine to 18 years.</p>
<p>The company said it received financing for four aircraft.</p>
<p>Two new Boeing Co 757 aircraft were financed under 18-year U.S. leveraged leases, with enhanced equipment trust certificates comprising the debt portion in three classes.</p>
<p>Two Boeing 727s, financed under nine-year leases, were revamped to meet Federal Aviation Administration-mandated noise restrictions.</p>
<p>This completes eight 727-200 conversions, it added.</p>
<p>A new Rolls-Royce Plc spare engine was financed separately for fifteen years.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
